# netsurf: DOM interface objects shaped as the spec's; URL-shaped objects stringify to their URL
#
# Found by the scorecard's JS error census (roadmap WS-B3):
# - "cannot read property 'prototype' of undefined" on BBC, the Guardian
#   (Sourcepoint's consent script patches [Element, CharacterData,
#   DocumentType].prototype), old.reddit (its web-components polyfill takes
#   Node.prototype.appendChild) and MDN (Lit reads Document.prototype).
#   Elements here carry their methods on per-tag prototypes and several
#   interface constructors did not exist. Now every method/accessor an
#   element, text node or document has is also on its spec interface
#   prototype (Node, Element, CharacterData, EventTarget -- the same native
#   functions, so .call() on any node works and a page patching those
#   prototypes stays harmless), and the missing interfaces exist as
#   "Illegal constructor" functions with the live objects' prototypes set
#   so instanceof holds: Document, HTMLDocument, DocumentType,
#   ProcessingInstruction, CDATASection, StyleSheet (CSSStyleSheet's
#   parent), CSSStyleRule, Location, Navigator, Screen, Performance, Crypto,
#   CustomElementRegistry, Storage. SubtleCrypto stays absent (absent beats
#   fake).
# - "TypeError: Invalid URL: [object Object]" on Wikipedia, ArchWiki, the
#   Python docs and MDN: location and <a>/<area> stringified to
#   "[object Object]", so new URL(location) threw, and document.baseURI was
#   undefined. They stringify to their href now; document.baseURI (honouring
#   <base href>), document.URL and document.documentURI are defined.
# The event methods (add/removeEventListener, dispatchEvent) are never
# copied onto interface prototypes, and nothing is copied onto
# Document.prototype: the bridge installs document's listener shims with
# `document.addEventListener = document.addEventListener || ...`, and an
# element's native one found through the new prototype took their place and
# registered nothing (the first version of this patch: JS-event-order 0/5).
# Test: JS-interfaces.html 8/8; JS-event-order.html 5/5.
